CoreCLR's copy of libunwind on witos (plan step R3.1): the PAL unwinds native frames through it, and its stepper calls
the OS part (os-linux.c), which Linux builds; witos builds the same source, whose /proc reader for the image of an
address fails explicitly there.
On release/8.0 (plan step N3.2) the change is the same.

